 Oct 12, Wood County&rsquo;s record runs 75 years, 1951 to 2025, on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids. November to December came in under 90% of normal in 36 of those years, the most of any pair. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 142% of normal in April to May and 31% in August to September. Every grid had its driest year in 1963, and grid 25687 fell to 59% that year.</p>"}
